  "Main topic of the publication": "This study investigates the impact of maternal immune activation (MIA) on placental and fetal brain development in mice by analyzing cytokine and mRNA content in placental and brain tissues after exposing pregnant dams to polyinosinic: polycytidylic acid (poly I:C). The findings suggest that MIA contributes to sex-specific abnormalities observed in neurodevelopmental disorders like ASD, potentially through altered neuronal development due to inflammatory cytokines.",
